B) COVARIANCE MATRIX OF THE RESONANCE PARAMETERS (MF=32)          9040 1451
   Below 4 keV - L.C. Leal (ORNL) by using the SAMMY code         9040 1451
                                                                  9040 1451
   From 4 to 100 keV - P. Schillebeeckx, I. Sirakov (IRMM, INRNE) 9040 1451
                                                                  9040 1451
  The covariance matrix of the average resonance parameters in    9040 1451
the unresolved resonance region was deduced from the covariance   9040 1451
matrix of the experimental data and the sensitivity matrix or the 9040 1451
partial derivatives with respect to the adjusted parameters.      9040 1451
The covariance matrix of the experimental data was constructed by 9040 1451
assuming the following uncertainties:                             9040 1451
                                                                  9040 1451
total cross section:                                              9040 1451
  - correlated          : 1.0%                                    9040 1451
  - uncorrelated        : 0.5%                                    9040 1451
                                                                  9040 1451
capture cross section                                             9040 1451
  - correlated          : 1.5%                                    9040 1451
  - uncorrelated        : 1.5%                                    9040 1451
                                                                  9040 1451
The sensitivity matrix was deduced with RECENT around the final   9040 1451
average resonance parameters used to construct File 2.            9040 1451
The covariance and sensivitivy matrix were constructed at the     9040 1451
energy points of the cross section data in File 3.                9040 1451
                                                                  9040 1451
Since in the fitting procedure only the neutron strength functions9040 1451
Sl for l = 0, 1 and 2 and the radiation widths Gg,l for l = 0,1   9040 1451
were adjusted, only the partial derivatives with respect to these 9040 1451
parameters were considered. The resulting covariance matrix of the9040 1451
adjusted parameters is:                                           9040 1451
                                                                  9040 1451
     Parameter    Rel. Unc.             Correlation matrix        9040 1451
                                                                  9040 1451
  S0    8.78E-5     2.0%     1.00   -0.61    0.86   -0.54    0.73 9040 1451
  Gg,0  23.6 meV    4.2%             1.00   -0.64    0.69   -0.58 9040 1451
  S1    1.90E-4     4.1%                     1.00   -0.54    0.74 9040 1451
  Gg,1  22.7 meV    3.7%                             1.00   -0.86 9040 1451
  S2    1.27E-4     20.%                                     1.00 9040 1451
                                                                  9040 1451
This covariance matrix was used to create file 32.                9040 1451
To construct file 32 a very small relative uncertainty on the     9040 1451
level distance was introduced and it was assumed that the         9040 1451
relative covariance elements for the reduced neutron widths can be9040 1451
approximated by the relative covariance elements of the neutron   9040 1451
strength functions.                                               9040 1451
